---
layout: none
---
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{% comment %}
  Every page's .url and nothing else -- deliberately not the jekyll-sitemap
  gem (see CLAUDE.md's "No RSS/Atom feed" note for why a generic
  third-party template assuming specific field names is a real risk for
  this repo's arbitrary, per-site content model; a sitemap only needs
  .url, so this is simple enough to just write directly). Excludes the
  404 page and this file/robots.txt themselves (not real indexable
  pages) by name, which works the same for both static Jekyll pages and
  every Contentful-generated page (always literally named "index.html",
  so never matches any of these).
{% endcomment %}
{% assign sitemap_pages = site.pages | where_exp: "p", "p.name != '404.html' and p.name != 'sitemap.xml' and p.name != 'robots.txt'" %}
{% for p in sitemap_pages %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ p.url | absolute_url }}</loc>
  </url>
{% endfor %}
</urlset>
